  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To contribute to the 2017 national goal of reducing the morbidity and mortality attributable to malaria in the various epidemiological zones by two thirds of the 2007-2008 levels - Kenya (01-Oct-2015-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kenya, Malaria, The National Treasury &amp; Economic Planning of the Government of Kenya (TNT)This program has the following goals: To contribute to the 2017 national goal of reducing the morbidity and mortality attributable to malaria in the various epidemiological zones by two thirds of the 2007-2008 levels. The objectives of this program are: Objective 1: To achieve and sustain 100% LLIN ownership (1 net for 2 persons at risk) among people living in malaria endemic and epidemic prone areas up to 2016.  Objective 2: To have 100% of diagnosed malaria patients receiving effective treatment by 2016.  Objective 3: To increase knowledge and practices on key malaria prevention and treatment intervention for LLIN use and care seeking behaviour among people in endemic, epidemic-prone and seasonal-transmission areas to at least 80% by 2016.  Objective 4: To have at least 80% of all counties promptly reporting on key malaria (impact, outcome and output) indicators by 2016.  Objective 5: To support programme management at all levels for effective performance throughout the grant period</narrative>
  </description>
